<title>USA: FOB Gulf Grain -Soy, corn offers mostly flat to up.</title>
<headline>FOB Gulf Grain -Soy, corn offers mostly flat to up.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. FOB Gulf soybean and corn offers were mostly steady to higher while wheat values remained unchanged, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers cited fairly quiet export activity.</p>
<p>On the export front, the Commodity Credit Corp said it bought a total of 85,000 tonnes of U.S. yellow corn for donation to North Korea.</p>
<p>The shipment period was slated for August 1-September 10.</p>
<p>Also, the CCC said it was seeking 3,530 tonnes U.S. hard redwinter wheat for Honduras.  </p>
